<body>
  <GameNav />
  <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> &gt; <a href="/rooms-and-exits/">Rooms &amp; Exits</a> &gt; <a href="/rooms-and-exits/">Chapter 2</a> &gt; Level 2</nav>

  <main class="seo-section">
    <h1>Rooms &amp; Exits Chapter 2 Level 2 Walkthrough: Cinemas</h1>

    <div class="disclaimer">Unofficial fan-made guide. Not affiliated with Webelinx Games, the developer of Rooms &amp; Exits: Escape Room Games.</div>

    <div class="verify-note">Rebuilt frame by frame from a recorded playthrough of the current build (Chapter 2, Level 2, "Cinemas"). 5 minutes 51 seconds of footage, extracted at one frame per second, read at full resolution and then re-read at 2× on the puzzle screens. The two numbers below that actually gate progress — the three menu prices and 3581 — were each read twice from separate frames. Where the recording cannot settle a detail, this page says so instead of guessing.</div>

    <div class="answer-box">
      <span class="label">Quick answer</span>
      <p>The only four-digit code in Cinemas is <b>3581</b>, and it is not visible when you first walk in. It appears on the <b>BURNING CITY</b> poster in the lobby after you put the fire on that poster out. Type it into the keypad on the red exit door and the level ends at <b>+50 coins</b>.</p>
      <ol>
        <li>Lobby, snack shelf above counter 1: take the <b>cable</b> out of the crisp bags.</li>
        <li>Lobby wall, wooden rack: use the <b>selfie stick</b> to knock the <b>key</b> off the middle peg.</li>
        <li>Price boards over the counters read <b>MENU 1 = 8</b>, <b>MENU 2 = 11</b>, <b>MENU 3 = 13</b>.</li>
        <li>Terminal under MENU 1: type <b>8+11+13</b> and press <b>=</b>.</li>
        <li>Hallway, red wall cabinet with a glass front: take the <b>fire extinguisher</b>.</li>
        <li>Use it on the <b>BURNING CITY</b> poster → <b>3581</b> → exit-door keypad → <b>+50 coins</b>.</li>
      </ol>
    </div>

    <div class="video-wrap">
            <div class="yt-facade" data-yt="kEZFGH2_GwY" data-title="Rooms &amp;amp; Exits Chapter 2 Level 2 Cinemas walkthrough"
           role="button" tabindex="0" aria-label="Play video: Rooms &amp;amp; Exits Chapter 2 Level 2 Cinemas walkthrough">
        <img src="https://i.ytimg.com/vi/kEZFGH2_GwY/maxresdefault.jpg"
             alt="Rooms &amp;amp; Exits Chapter 2 Level 2 Cinemas walkthrough" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1280" height="720"
             onerror="this.onerror=null;this.src='https://i.ytimg.com/vi/kEZFGH2_GwY/hqdefault.jpg'">
      </div>
    </div>

    <img class="hero" src="/rooms-and-exits/c2l2-hero-lobby.jpg" alt="Rooms and Exits Chapter 2 Level 2 Cinemas: the lobby with the BURNING CITY poster, the CINEMA sign, three numbered counters and the rope queue" width="1200" height="594" />

    <h2>What Cinemas actually is<span class="accent">.</span></h2>
    <p>Cinemas is the second level of Chapter 2, "No Honor Among Thieves", and it is a building rather than a room. You get a lobby with a concession counter split into three numbered stations, a snack wall behind it, a queue of red ropes on a black-and-white tiled floor, and a big <b>BURNING CITY</b> poster hanging on the left-hand wall. Off to the right is the entrance to the screens, and behind that a hallway with the EXIT doors, three film posters, a narrow ticket kiosk and a red wall cabinet.</p>
    <p>The screens themselves are ordinary cinemas: rows of red seats, a blank white screen, a red exit door in the corner. One of them has 3D glasses lying on the seats. The other is where the projection shows you a strip of arrows.</p>
    <p>What makes this level awkward is the order. There is only one number puzzle in the whole thing — the four digits on the burnt poster — but the poster is <em>on fire</em> when you arrive, so the code does not exist yet. The thing that puts the fire out is a fire extinguisher in a wall cabinet in a different room, and nothing in the lobby points you at it. Meanwhile the lobby itself hands you three separate price boards, a calculator terminal, a seat chart and two other key screens, and none of them announces what it is for. That is why the level feels much longer than it is: most of the time goes on working out which screen is a puzzle and which is scenery.</p>
    <p>Our recording finishes it in 8 minutes 9 seconds of in-game time — the figure the game itself prints on the completion screen — and the footage is 5:51, because the recorder cut the dead time. Every timestamp on this page is a timestamp in that video, not in the game clock.</p>

    <h2>Step by step<span class="accent">.</span></h2>
    <p>The steps below are in the order you meet them walking the building: lobby, hallway, screen 1, then the exit door. The timestamps point at the moment each action appears in the recording; our recorder doubles back constantly, so the minute marks are not in ascending order.</p>

    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 1 · 0:02</span>
      <strong>Read the lobby before you touch anything</strong>
      The opening shot is the whole level in one frame, and it is worth ten seconds of your time. Left wall: <b>BURNING CITY</b>. Back wall: the red <b>CINEMA</b> sign with five lit boards under it — 3D CINEMA, MENU 1, MENU 2, MENU 3, TOP MOVIES. Counter: three red stations numbered <b>1</b>, <b>2</b> and <b>3</b>, each with its own monitor, popcorn cases between them. Behind the counter: the <b>EXPRESS CAFE</b> sign over a wall of crisp bags, two coffee machines on the right, two glass-door fridges of bottles at either end. Right wall: the <b>ENT</b> doorway into the screens.
      <img src="/rooms-and-exits/c2l2-hero-lobby.jpg" alt="The Cinemas lobby in Rooms and Exits Chapter 2 Level 2, with the BURNING CITY poster, CINEMA sign and numbered counters" width="1200" height="594" loading="lazy" />
      <div class="ts">Watch: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kEZFGH2_GwY&t=2s" target="_blank" rel="noopener">0:02</a></div>
    </div>
    <InContentAd />

    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 2 · 0:13</span>
      <strong>The cable is inside the crisp bags</strong>
      Walk behind counter 1 and zoom on the snack wall under the EXPRESS CAFE sign. Three bags fill the frame — a pale <b>POTATO CHIPS</b> bag on the left, two green <b>CHIPS</b> bags on the right — and a white coiled USB cable is lying across the front of them. Tap it and the pickup caption reads <b>Cable</b>.
      <img src="/rooms-and-exits/c2l2-chips-shelf.jpg" alt="The crisp bag shelf behind counter 1 where the cable is hidden in Cinemas" width="1200" height="594" loading="lazy" />
      <div class="ts">Watch: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kEZFGH2_GwY&t=13s" target="_blank" rel="noopener">0:13</a></div>
    </div>

    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 3 · 0:15</span>
      <strong>Log it and move on</strong>
      The cable is the single most-missed item in the level, because the shelf reads as decoration and the bag art is loud enough to hide a white cable lying on top of it. Nothing in the level tells you what it is for at the point you find it, and the pickup screen gives you one word. Take it and go back out to the lobby floor.
      <img src="/rooms-and-exits/c2l2-cable.jpg" alt="The Cable pickup screen in Rooms and Exits Cinemas" width="1200" height="594" loading="lazy" />
      <div class="ts">Watch: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kEZFGH2_GwY&t=15s" target="_blank" rel="noopener">0:15</a></div>
    </div>

    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 4 · 0:38</span>
      <strong>The key on the rack, and why you need the selfie stick</strong>
      On the lobby wall, between the poster and the counter, there is a wooden bar with three pegs. A single silver key hangs on the <b>middle</b> peg, high enough that tapping it does nothing — the hot zone only responds once you have something long enough. Select the <b>selfie stick</b> from your inventory and use it on the rack: the stick telescopes up, hooks the ring and the key drops into your inventory with the label <b>Key</b> at 0:41. Two items, two different screens, and the game never connects them for you.
      <img src="/rooms-and-exits/c2l2-key-rack.jpg" alt="The wooden peg rack in the lobby with the key that has to be reached with the selfie stick" width="1200" height="594" loading="lazy" />
      <div class="ts">Watch: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kEZFGH2_GwY&t=38s" target="_blank" rel="noopener">0:38</a></div>
    </div>

    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 5 · 1:36</span>
      <strong>The ticket desk and its printer</strong>
      Behind counter 2 there is a red desk with the terminal setup: a monitor showing a flat blue screen with a grey question-mark button in the corner, a full keyboard, a mouse and, on the left, a grey ticket printer with paper already sitting in the slot. This desk is where the level's one printable item comes from — a <b>CINEMA TICKET</b> naming the theatre and the seat. Our footage never shows the cable being plugged in anywhere, so treat "the cable goes here" as the obvious reading rather than something the recording proves.
      <img src="/rooms-and-exits/c2l2-ticket-desk.jpg" alt="The ticket desk in Cinemas: monitor, keyboard, mouse and the ticket printer" width="1200" height="594" loading="lazy" />
      <div class="ts">Watch: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kEZFGH2_GwY&t=96s" target="_blank" rel="noopener">1:36</a></div>
    </div>

    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 6 · 1:54</span>
      <strong>Find screen 1</strong>
      Through the ENT doorway on the right you are in the hallway: black-and-white tiled floor, EXIT double doors on the left under a red sign, a red wall cabinet on the same wall, and two sets of red double doors on the back wall with glowing numbers over them and white up-arrows on the doors. Between them hang three posters — <b>FREE POPCORN</b>, <b>Love Stories movie collection</b>, <b>BEST FILM MARATHON</b> — with a slim grey kiosk in front of the middle one and a plant on the right. The door marked <b>1</b> is the screen you can get into.
      <img src="/rooms-and-exits/c2l2-hallway.jpg" alt="The Cinemas hallway with the EXIT doors, red wall cabinet and the doors numbered 1 and 2" width="1200" height="594" loading="lazy" />
      <div class="ts">Watch: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kEZFGH2_GwY&t=114s" target="_blank" rel="noopener">1:54</a></div>
    </div>

    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 7 · 4:00</span>
      <strong>The terminal under MENU 1: 8 + 11 + 13</strong>
      This is the one arithmetic screen in the level and it is easy to read as a shop till. The left half of the screen shows the <b>MENU 1</b> combo board — the popcorn bucket and drink you saw over the counter. The right half is a calculator: digits 1–9, a zero, plus, minus, C and equals. Our recording types <b>8+11+13</b> straight into the display and presses <b>=</b>.
      <img src="/rooms-and-exits/c2l2-terminal-sum.jpg" alt="The MENU 1 terminal in Cinemas with the calculator showing 8+11+13" width="1200" height="594" loading="lazy" />
      <p>Where the numbers come from is the part nobody spots: they are the price tags on the three boards above the counters, printed in red and blue circles with two small zeros in superscript. <b>MENU 1 = 8.00</b>, <b>MENU 2 = 11.00</b>, <b>MENU 3 = 13.00</b> — so 8, 11 and 13. One board on its own tells you nothing; the sum of all three is what the terminal is asking for. Add them yourself and you get 32, and the keypad in our recording takes the plain integers with no decimal point.</p>
      <div class="ts">Watch: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kEZFGH2_GwY&t=240s" target="_blank" rel="noopener">4:00</a></div>
    </div>

    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 8 · 2:20</span>
      <strong>The seat chart, and the ticket that names your seat</strong>
      The terminal also opens a seat chart: six rows lettered <b>A</b> to <b>F</b> from the bottom up, twelve seats numbered <b>1</b> to <b>12</b> across, each seat drawn as a little U. Tapping one fills it solid red. Our recording works this screen twice, marks seats in several rows and then backs out to the lobby.
      <img src="/rooms-and-exits/c2l2-seat-map.jpg" alt="The cinema seat chart in Cinemas with six rows A to F and twelve seats per row, a few marked red" width="1200" height="594" loading="lazy" />
      <p>The seat to use is on the ticket the printer at the desk produces at 4:32: <b>THEATER : 01 / SEAT : E11</b>, with DATE 10/07, PRICE 10 USD and the title line reading <b>MOVIE 3D</b>. So the chart is row <b>E</b>, seat <b>11</b> — the fifth row up from the bottom and the eleventh seat across. That number is legible at full resolution and we have read it from three separate frames, which is more than can be said for the chart itself: the marked cells on our copy are too small to enumerate reliably, and the recording marks more than one seat, so we cannot tell you whether the chart checks only E11 or the whole pattern of red cells.</p>
      <img src="/rooms-and-exits/c2l2-ticket.jpg" alt="The CINEMA TICKET printed in Cinemas, showing THEATER 01 and SEAT E11" width="1200" height="594" loading="lazy" />
      <div class="ts">Watch: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kEZFGH2_GwY&t=140s" target="_blank" rel="noopener">2:20</a> · ticket at <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kEZFGH2_GwY&t=272s" target="_blank" rel="noopener">4:32</a></div>
    </div>

    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 9 · 2:36</span>
      <strong>Screen 1: the 3D glasses on the seats</strong>
      Inside screen 1 the camera looks down the rows to a blank white screen, with a red exit door in the far corner. On the seats in the near rows there are two things worth tapping: a pair of anaglyph <b>3D glasses</b> (white frame, blue and red lenses) and a red-and-white striped popcorn bucket. The glasses are labelled <b>3d glasses</b> on the pickup screen and go straight into your inventory — from then on the icon sits in the top-right corner of the HUD, which is how you can tell at a glance that you are carrying them.
      <img src="/rooms-and-exits/c2l2-auditorium-3d.jpg" alt="The 3D glasses pickup on the seats in screen 1 of Cinemas" width="1200" height="594" loading="lazy" />
      <div class="ts">Watch: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kEZFGH2_GwY&t=156s" target="_blank" rel="noopener">2:36</a></div>
    </div>

    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 10 · 4:54</span>
      <strong>The screen changes</strong>
      Come back into the auditorium later and the projection has changed: instead of a blank white rectangle the screen is showing a cartoon sunset over water — pink and orange sky, palm trees on the right, a white curl of surf across the middle — with a row of white arrows laid into the sky above the sun. This is a clue, not a cutscene. It is the only place in the level where the game shows you a pattern and expects you to carry it somewhere else.
      <img src="/rooms-and-exits/c2l2-screen-arrows.jpg" alt="The cinema screen in Cinemas showing a sunset image with a row of white arrows" width="1200" height="594" loading="lazy" />
      <div class="ts">Watch: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kEZFGH2_GwY&t=294s" target="_blank" rel="noopener">4:54</a></div>
    </div>

    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 11 · 4:58</span>
      <strong>The five-bar panel</strong>
      Somewhere in the building there is a panel set into a red frame: five vertical yellow bars with horizontal ribs, each on a black stem, and a round silver button with a hand icon underneath. The bars slide up and down; the button submits. The arrows on the cinema screen are the only pattern the level ever shows you and this is the only five-slot control in the building, so the two belong together — but our copy of the panel never sits still long enough at one frame per second to record a bar-by-bar target, and the one clear frame we have (5:01) shows the bars already at mixed heights, which tells us what the panel looks like mid-solve, not what it wants.
      <img src="/rooms-and-exits/c2l2-bar-panel.jpg" alt="The five yellow bars and hand button on the panel in Cinemas" width="1200" height="594" loading="lazy" />
      <div class="ts">Watch: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kEZFGH2_GwY&t=298s" target="_blank" rel="noopener">4:58</a></div>
    </div>

    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 12 · 5:04</span>
      <strong>The extinguisher cabinet</strong>
      In the hallway, mounted on the wall among the red doors and posters, there is a red cabinet with a glass front. Its door swings open to the left and a red <b>fire extinguisher</b> is clipped upright inside, with a black hose and a cone horn. Tap it and the caption reads <b>Fire extinguisher</b>. This is the item that makes the level's only code exist, and it is in a completely different room from the poster it is used on.
      <img src="/rooms-and-exits/c2l2-extinguisher.jpg" alt="The red fire extinguisher inside the open wall cabinet in the Cinemas hallway" width="1200" height="594" loading="lazy" />
      <div class="ts">Watch: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kEZFGH2_GwY&t=304s" target="_blank" rel="noopener">5:04</a></div>
    </div>

    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 13 · 5:34</span>
      <strong>Put the poster out</strong>
      Go back to the lobby and face the <b>BURNING CITY</b> poster — the one with the red-and-yellow striped tape on two silver stanchions in front of it. Select the extinguisher and use it. The game cuts to a framed close-up of the nozzle spraying foam across the poster while the flames wash off it, and the shot holds there while the poster chars.
      <img src="/rooms-and-exits/c2l2-poster-fire.jpg" alt="Using the fire extinguisher on the burning BURNING CITY poster in the Cinemas lobby" width="1200" height="594" loading="lazy" />
      <div class="ts">Watch: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kEZFGH2_GwY&t=334s" target="_blank" rel="noopener">5:34</a></div>
    </div>

    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 14 · 5:38</span>
      <strong>3581</strong>
      As the smoke clears, four big digits are left burned into the poster: <b>3 · 5 · 8 · 1</b>, in a horizontal row, left to right. This is the only code in Cinemas and it is worth writing down as it appears — it is on screen for a couple of seconds before the camera pulls back out of the close-up.
      <img src="/rooms-and-exits/c2l2-code-3581.jpg" alt="The code 3581 revealed on the burnt BURNING CITY poster in Cinemas" width="1200" height="594" loading="lazy" />
      <div class="ts">Watch: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kEZFGH2_GwY&t=338s" target="_blank" rel="noopener">5:38</a></div>
    </div>

    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 15 · 5:46</span>
      <strong>The exit door keypad</strong>
      The keypad is on the red double door marked EXIT in the hallway — the door on the left under the red EXIT sign, not the numbered screen doors. It is a plain 4-by-3 pad: 1 to 9, then X, 0 and a tick. Type <b>3581</b>. The display shows the digits as you enter them, so check that it reads 3581 before you press the tick; if it does not, X clears the field. Press the tick and the door opens on the completion screen.
      <img src="/rooms-and-exits/c2l2-keypad.jpg" alt="The exit door keypad in Cinemas with 3581 entered" width="1200" height="594" loading="lazy" />
      <div class="ts">Watch: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kEZFGH2_GwY&t=346s" target="_blank" rel="noopener">5:46</a></div>
    </div>

    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 16 · 5:50</span>
      <strong>Level complete: +50 coins</strong>
      The level closes on the <b>LEVEL COMPLETED!</b> screen. The top reward panel pays <b>+50</b> coins and prints your level time — 8:09 in our run. Under it is the piggy bank panel with its own reward. Those coins go into the balance in the top-left of the HUD; the level has nothing else to collect.
      <img src="/rooms-and-exits/c2l2-complete.jpg" alt="The LEVEL COMPLETED screen for Chapter 2 Level 2 Cinemas with a +50 coin reward" width="1200" height="594" loading="lazy" />
